The '''Aurelius system''' is a gravitationally bound planetary system consisting of the luminous G0V main-sequence star [[Aurelius]] and the extensive retinue of celestial objects orbiting within its gravitational and heliospheric domain.<ref name="IACC_Overview">Inter-Adonian Celestial Commission (IACC). (2022). *Compendium of Planetary Geodesy and Dynamical Ephemerides of the Aurelius System*. Annals of Astronomical Geodesy, 51(1), 1–64.</ref> The system comprises twelve recognized major planetary bodies—seven inner terrestrial worlds, two massive gas giants, two outer ice giants, and one trans-Centinelan dwarf planet—alongside dozens of natural satellites, ring systems, asteroidal belts, and cometary reservoirs.<ref name="Tanigaki_Arch">Tanigaki, R. (2018). *Architecture of the Heavens: Orbital Resonance and Gravitational Equilibrium in the Aurelius System*. University of Okami Academic Press, pp. 24–88.</ref>

The system's dynamical architecture is organized into four distinct radial provinces. The Inner Terrestrial Realm (0.20 to 1.60 AU) is anchored by the sun-scorched iron world [[Tartessos]], the super-greenhouse world [[Ciguapa]], the tidally locked lava-ice world [[Mictlán]], the hot sub-Neptune [[Quetzal]], the life-bearing crown jewel [[Adonia]], and the canyon-scarred red desert world [[Aztlán]]. The Frost-Line Transition (1.60 to 4.00 AU) is defined by the cryogenic desert world [[Cíbola]] and the main asteroid belt, marking the boundary where volatile water, carbon dioxide, and methane condense into solid ice. Beyond lies the Realm of the Giants (5.00 to 36.00 AU), dominated by the system's gravitational sentinels—the regal violet gas giant [[Amatista]], the tilted colossus [[Alcázar]] (possessing 510 Adonian masses with an extreme 97.8° axial tilt), the serene alabaster ice giant [[Lucero]], and the cobalt-blue ice giant [[Centinela]]. Finally, the Outer Kuiper Frontier (36.00 to 125.00+ AU) encompasses the trans-Centinelan debris disk known as the Sentinel Belt, anchored by the coal-black binary dwarf planet [[Erebo]] and terminating at the Aureliopause boundary against the interstellar medium.<ref name="IACC_Overview" />

The hallmark of the Aurelius system is its extraordinary long-term dynamical equilibrium, governed by two interconnected gravitational pillars: the inner clockwork resonance between Quetzal and Adonia (a precise 5:4 orbital resonance that structures Adonia's tides, climate, and leap-year calendar without destabilizing its circular orbit), and the outer gravitational shielding provided by Amatista and Alcázar, whose immense masses sweep incoming debris and protect the inner biosphere from catastrophic impact bombardment.<ref name="Aldana_Equilibrium">Aldana, E. (2023). *Secular Orbital Stability and Resonance Lock in Multi-Planet Systems with Low-Density Hot Giants*. Castejón Astrophysical Review, 88(3), 210–248.</ref>

